  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nGiven the below HTML Chromium does not execute the script element but Firefox does. I *think* Chromium is correct here but want to make sure my understanding is correct.\n\nI believe Firefox is erroneously going down the [children changed steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#the-script-element:concept-node-children-changed-ext:~:text=script%20children%20changed%20steps) path for script, even though moveBefore does not call it.\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<body>\n    <div id=\"source\" hidden>alert('executed')</div>\n    <div id=\"target\"><script id=\"script\"></script></div>\n\n    <script>\n        const target = document.getElementById(\"script-target\");\n\n        const textNode = source.firstChild;\n\n        script.moveBefore(textNode, null);\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```",
